# Convex functions

Public functions use `v.*` args. Mutations that write call `requireUserId` from `convex/lib/auth.ts`. List queries may return `[]` when signed out instead of throwing.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — scan then filter
const all = await ctx.db.query("messages").collect();
return all.filter((m) => m.channelId === args.channelId);

// ✅ GOOD — use the schema index
return await ctx.db
  .query("messages")
  .withIndex("by_channel", (q) => q.eq("channelId", args.channelId))
  .order("desc")
  .take(50);
```

- Do not put presence rows in `schema.ts`; wrap `@convex-dev/presence` in `convex/presence.ts`
- Typing uses the `typing` table + `ctx.scheduler.runAfter` → `internal.typing.clearIfStale`
- Keep presence `list` room-scoped (no viewer id in args) so clients share the query cache
- Edit `convex/schema.ts` when adding tables; never treat Postgres/SQLite as the app schema
- Do not hand-edit `convex/_generated/` — `npx convex dev` regenerates it
